        "ImageDescription": {
          "value": "A giant gamma-ray structure emerges by processing Fermi all-sky data at energies from 1 to 10 GeV. The dumbbell-shaped feature emerges from the galactic center and extends 50 degrees north and south from the plane of the Milky Way. A supermassive black hole weighing about 4 million times the sun's mass also lurks in the galactic center; these \"gamma-ray bubbles\" may have arisen as a result of a past eruption by the black hole or another source near the galactic center.",
          "source": "commons-desc-page"
